[size=5]Installation[/size]

[b]1 — Frameworks[/b]
Install the mods in the [b]Requirements[/b] tab first. The seven hard ones are all standard frameworks; without any of them the mod does not compile at launch.
[b]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/b] is listed as optional, but it is where you enter your API key. Install it.

[b]2 — ai_npc[/b]
Vortex or MO2: install the archive and let the FOMOD run. It asks one question — which provider the characters should use. Answer [b]OpenRouter[/b].
By hand: unzip the archive at the Cyberpunk 2077 root.

[b]3 — An OpenRouter key[/b]
Create one at [url=https://openrouter.ai/keys]openrouter.ai/keys[/url] and put a few dollars on the account. At the recommended model, two hours of play a day costs well under a dollar a month.
The mod talks to OpenRouter directly from your game. Nothing goes through me, and the key never leaves your machine.

[b]4 — Three clicks in game[/b]
Launch the game, open the CET overlay and find the [b]AI NPC[/b] window, tab [b]Setup[/b]. Everything you need is circled in red below:
[list=1]
[*]set the provider to [b]OpenRouter[/b]
[*]paste your key in the field and press [b]Save[/b]
[*]press [b]Test connection[/b]
[/list]
[img]INSTALL_SCREENSHOT_URL[/img]
[i]Test connection[/i] sends one real request through the same code a character's reply uses, and prints what came back. If it prints an answer, you are done — no restart. If it prints an error, that error is the provider's own, and it tells you what to fix.

[b]5 — Which model[/b]
The shipped default is free, and throttled by whoever serves it: measured, it answered 8 requests out of 54. It is there so you can see the mod work, not so you can play an evening.
Paste one of these in the [b]Model[/b] field instead:
[list]
[*][b]qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507[/b] — ~0.55 $/month at two hours a day. The default pick.
[*][b]meta-llama/llama-4-maverick[/b] — ~2.56 $/month. Pick this one if you lower the content level, which it is the only model measured to actually respect.
[*][b]deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324[/b] — ~3.21 $/month. Fallback when a provider is down.
[/list]
Do not pick on price alone: a cheap model can write a perfect reply and silently drop the command that makes a character show up somewhere. Ten models were measured against four criteria — the table is in the mod's documentation.
